1
00:00:17,455 --> 00:00:18,455
Dear.

2
00:00:20,037 --> 00:00:20,783
Den!

3
00:00:20,842 --> 00:00:21,842
Dear.

4
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:24,581
Help me.

5
00:00:24,888 --> 00:00:26,029
Den, where are you?

6
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,890
I'm trapped in here.

7
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,020
Den!

8
00:00:31,938 --> 00:00:33,909
I'm here. Den, where are you?

9
00:00:34,685 --> 00:00:35,685
Dear.

10
00:00:36,689 --> 00:00:38,151
Den, I'm here.

11
00:00:40,057 --> 00:00:41,057
Dear.

12
00:00:43,902 --> 00:00:44,902
Dear.

13
00:00:45,826 --> 00:00:46,826
Den.

14
00:00:50,063 --> 00:00:51,063
Den.

15
00:01:06,627 --> 00:01:07,627
Dear.

16
00:01:08,305 --> 00:01:08,670
Dear.

17
00:01:08,847 --> 00:01:09,847
Den.

18
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:10,348
Den.

19
00:01:10,648 --> 00:01:11,648
Dear, help me.

20
00:01:13,174 --> 00:01:13,690
Den.

21
00:01:13,853 --> 00:01:14,853
Blood.

22
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,293
I'm here, Den.

23
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,600
Den!

24
00:01:53,489 --> 00:01:54,489
Who's there?

25
00:01:54,918 --> 00:01:56,700
I'm here to make a delivery.

26
00:02:22,576 --> 00:02:23,576
What are you doing here?

27
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,668
It's my day off, so I thought I'd drop by.

28
00:02:28,581 --> 00:02:29,581
And...

29
00:02:30,398 --> 00:02:31,398
What's this?

30
00:02:33,923 --> 00:02:34,923
I got it for you.

31
00:02:46,661 --> 00:02:48,939
Have you always lived alone, Dear?

32
00:02:51,909 --> 00:02:52,909
Yeah.

33
00:02:53,057 --> 00:02:54,558
That must get lonely.

34
00:02:56,210 --> 00:02:57,210
I'm used to it.

35
00:03:00,106 --> 00:03:02,026
Being used to it doesn't mean you're not lonely.

36
00:03:05,016 --> 00:03:07,210
So... you came here to keep me company?

37
00:03:11,015 --> 00:03:11,407
Yeah.

38
00:03:11,981 --> 00:03:12,981
Something like that.

39
00:03:24,293 --> 00:03:26,069
You remembered I like it less sweet.

40
00:03:26,297 --> 00:03:27,297
Well?

41
00:03:27,518 --> 00:03:28,678
Pretty thoughtful of me, huh?

42
00:03:42,523 --> 00:03:43,523
What are you staring at?

43
00:03:45,317 --> 00:03:46,317
Nothing.

44
00:03:48,052 --> 00:03:49,052
Thanks.

45
00:03:55,239 --> 00:03:56,822
Then I'm staying for a while today.

46
00:03:58,822 --> 00:03:59,938
Who said you could?

47
00:04:01,081 --> 00:04:02,081
Well...

48
00:04:02,295 --> 00:04:03,966
You already took the milk tea.

49
00:04:04,246 --> 00:04:05,408
So you owe me one.

50
00:04:08,987 --> 00:04:10,874
Is this any good? Is it?

51
00:05:14,126 --> 00:05:15,126
Hello.

52
00:05:17,501 --> 00:05:19,738
I'm only half an hour late. Don't hold it against me.

53
00:05:21,378 --> 00:05:22,378
Nava's asleep.

54
00:05:22,845 --> 00:05:24,624
You can wait outside the room and keep watch.

55
00:05:24,648 --> 00:05:25,648
Oh.

56
00:05:25,966 --> 00:05:26,966
Sure.

57
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,660
Here you go.

58
00:05:40,731 --> 00:05:41,573
You should get to work.

59
00:05:41,676 --> 00:05:43,510
Don't worry about Nava. I'll look after her.

60
00:05:44,752 --> 00:05:45,752
Okay.

61
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,760
Aren't you going in? You'll be late.

62
00:06:45,361 --> 00:06:46,361
Don't worry.

63
00:06:46,943 --> 00:06:48,663
I don't think anything will happen tonight.

64
00:06:51,009 --> 00:06:52,530
When the lights turn blue,

65
00:06:52,531 --> 00:06:54,571
it means the period is safe.

66
00:06:54,834 --> 00:06:57,628
No customers will enter the store during this time.

67
00:06:58,294 --> 00:06:59,488
It's really safe, right?

68
00:07:04,461 --> 00:07:05,461
Yeah.

69
00:07:05,936 --> 00:07:07,379
Usually, nothing happens.

70
00:07:08,345 --> 00:07:09,345
But in the past...

71
00:07:10,309 --> 00:07:12,555
these blue lights came on even more often.

72
00:07:17,817 --> 00:07:19,057
It’s the quiet nights like this

73
00:07:20,532 --> 00:07:21,532
that are scarier.

74
00:07:21,981 --> 00:07:22,981
Scarier?

75
00:07:25,264 --> 00:07:26,974
They make you paranoid.

76
00:07:28,191 --> 00:07:29,191
The less that happens,

77
00:07:31,089 --> 00:07:31,999
the more it feels like

78
00:07:32,023 --> 00:07:34,143
something could jump out and attack us at any moment.

79
00:07:41,021 --> 00:07:42,033
You're still here

80
00:07:43,965 --> 00:07:45,205
because of your brother, right?

81
00:07:57,365 --> 00:07:59,199
Den used to work the night shift here.

82
00:08:01,889 --> 00:08:02,933
Then one night...

83
00:08:04,304 --> 00:08:05,433
he never came back.

84
00:08:09,108 --> 00:08:10,413
I asked Cherd about it once,

85
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:13,499
but all he said was...

86
00:08:16,317 --> 00:08:17,877
Den disappeared before his shift ended.

87
00:08:23,262 --> 00:08:24,262
In the end...

88
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:26,816
I came to work here

89
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,710
hoping I might find him or learn something.

90
00:08:31,483 --> 00:08:32,483
What if..

91
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:33,919
You never find anything?

92
00:08:35,144 --> 00:08:37,331
Are you going to keep working here forever?

93
00:08:38,943 --> 00:08:40,007
Aren't you scared?

94
00:08:42,937 --> 00:08:44,380
I might have been scared before,

95
00:08:46,478 --> 00:08:47,633
but now I'm used to it.

96
00:08:49,813 --> 00:08:50,813
Trust me.

97
00:08:51,074 --> 00:08:52,154
You'll get used to it, too.

98
00:09:07,074 --> 00:09:08,914
Okay, this side's done. Give me the other one.

99
00:09:15,125 --> 00:09:16,125
What happened to you?

100
00:09:18,115 --> 00:09:19,115
Does it hurt?

101
00:09:23,509 --> 00:09:24,638
Nava, answer me.

102
00:09:50,328 --> 00:09:52,044
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

103
00:10:05,708 --> 00:10:06,708
Sergeant Wichian.

104
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:07,204
Hey.

105
00:10:07,406 --> 00:10:07,967
Captain.

106
00:10:08,261 --> 00:10:09,261
What are you doing here?

107
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:12,236
Oh, I've resigned from the police force.

108
00:10:12,491 --> 00:10:12,863
What?

109
00:10:13,385 --> 00:10:14,385
Why?

110
00:10:15,043 --> 00:10:16,401
Some family problems, sir.

111
00:10:17,302 --> 00:10:19,266
And now you're working at a store?

112
00:10:23,599 --> 00:10:24,337
All right.

113
00:10:24,618 --> 00:10:25,938
I don't mean to look down on you.

114
00:10:27,437 --> 00:10:28,978
Leaving the police force

115
00:10:29,389 --> 00:10:30,469
might even be for the best.

116
00:10:31,373 --> 00:10:32,476
Good cops

117
00:10:33,553 --> 00:10:34,553
die young.

118
00:10:37,801 --> 00:10:38,801
Your change is five baht.

119
00:10:41,509 --> 00:10:42,509
I'd better go.

120
00:10:43,331 --> 00:10:44,731
I have to keep patrolling the area.

121
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:50,018
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

122
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,123
You've been working here for a week now.

123
00:10:59,147 --> 00:11:00,147
How do you feel?

124
00:11:20,612 --> 00:11:22,694
Tell me how many cans you want. I'll get them.

125
00:11:26,892 --> 00:11:27,892
It's getting better.

126
00:11:28,941 --> 00:11:30,581
I don't get startled as easily as before.

127
00:11:34,992 --> 00:11:35,632
Excuse me.

128
00:11:35,919 --> 00:11:36,311
Yes?

129
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:38,058
One bag of porridge for a kid, please.

130
00:11:38,082 --> 00:11:39,191
Sure, coming right up.

131
00:11:39,882 --> 00:11:40,882
Hey.

132
00:11:41,311 --> 00:11:42,333
You don't live alone?

133
00:11:43,882 --> 00:11:44,352
No.

134
00:11:44,705 --> 00:11:45,945
Right, I live with my daughter.

135
00:11:46,141 --> 00:11:47,141
Seriously?

136
00:11:47,492 --> 00:11:48,492
You have a daughter?

137
00:11:52,101 --> 00:11:53,974
She's seven. Her name's Nava.

138
00:11:54,829 --> 00:11:55,829
What about her mother?

139
00:12:16,572 --> 00:12:17,212
Well...

140
00:12:17,525 --> 00:12:18,693
Why are you working here?

141
00:12:21,846 --> 00:12:22,846
Just what you guessed.

142
00:12:24,574 --> 00:12:25,574
I'm in debt,

143
00:12:26,507 --> 00:12:28,027
so I need to earn money to pay it off.

144
00:12:33,092 --> 00:12:34,092
Your porridge is ready.

145
00:12:34,471 --> 00:12:35,471
Thank you.

146
00:12:43,692 --> 00:12:44,692
Metha.

147
00:12:45,403 --> 00:12:46,403
Metha.

148
00:12:49,202 --> 00:12:50,202
What's up?

149
00:12:50,462 --> 00:12:51,462
Well...

150
00:12:52,569 --> 00:12:53,849
Do you still owe a lot of money?

151
00:12:55,213 --> 00:12:56,213
Why do you ask?

152
00:12:59,377 --> 00:13:00,591
If you need money,

153
00:13:01,972 --> 00:13:03,092
you can borrow some from me.

154
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,626
How could I let a kid like you help me?

155
00:13:13,224 --> 00:13:14,236
I can handle it myself.

156
00:13:16,997 --> 00:13:17,997
But still...

157
00:13:18,694 --> 00:13:19,694
thanks.

158
00:13:35,757 --> 00:13:37,473
Oh, let me tell you.

159
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:38,883
It's such a mess.

160
00:13:39,719 --> 00:13:40,783
Yeah, exactly.

161
00:13:41,011 --> 00:13:42,056
Poor kid.

162
00:13:42,347 --> 00:13:43,896
All she knows is that her mother ran away

163
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:44,920
and abandoned her.

164
00:13:45,630 --> 00:13:47,314
I feel so sorry for her.

165
00:13:47,549 --> 00:13:49,664
I really do. She hardly speaks.

166
00:13:50,173 --> 00:13:50,735
It's like...

167
00:13:51,074 --> 00:13:51,772
what do you call it?

168
00:13:52,014 --> 00:13:53,744
Oh, a troubled child.

169
00:13:53,882 --> 00:13:55,494
One of those mentally disturbed kids.

170
00:13:55,814 --> 00:13:56,814
Yeah.

171
00:13:57,162 --> 00:13:59,183
I don't know how he manages it.

172
00:13:59,495 --> 00:14:02,465
Besides, he's not even the child's real father.

173
00:14:02,951 --> 00:14:04,603
Okay, I have to go.

174
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,700
Oh.

175
00:14:06,855 --> 00:14:07,855
Metha.

176
00:14:08,386 --> 00:14:09,464
You're back.

177
00:14:10,981 --> 00:14:12,528
Nava's still asleep.

178
00:14:22,731 --> 00:14:24,441
What happened to the stuffed rabbit?

179
00:14:25,357 --> 00:14:25,690
Well...

180
00:14:26,134 --> 00:14:27,688
I thought it was old,

181
00:14:27,877 --> 00:14:30,357
so I was going to wash it, but Nava wouldn't let me.

182
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,036
She really loves that rabbit.

183
00:14:42,275 --> 00:14:43,346
I understand that.

184
00:14:43,581 --> 00:14:46,452
But some things should be thrown away.

185
00:14:46,477 --> 00:14:47,308
They clutter up the house.

186
00:14:47,401 --> 00:14:48,830
Or you could donate it.

187
00:14:48,994 --> 00:14:50,034
That would be a good deed.

188
00:14:52,701 --> 00:14:53,701
Well...

189
00:14:53,987 --> 00:14:55,012
I'll head home now.

190
00:14:56,618 --> 00:14:57,618
Okay.

191
00:15:05,831 --> 00:15:08,237
Ta-da. Mr. Rabbit.

192
00:15:24,782 --> 00:15:25,782
Don't worry.

193
00:15:26,982 --> 00:15:28,320
I will get it fixed.

194
00:15:30,043 --> 00:15:31,329
It will be as good as new.

195
00:15:36,779 --> 00:15:40,669
(Arunchai School)

196
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,335
Excuse me, Nava's father.

197
00:15:51,038 --> 00:15:52,918
There's something I'd like to discuss with you.

198
00:15:53,198 --> 00:15:54,608
Please come inside for a moment.

199
00:15:58,837 --> 00:16:00,462
I'd like to talk to you about Nava.

200
00:16:01,507 --> 00:16:02,721
From what I've observed,

201
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:04,973
Nava is very quiet.

202
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:06,560
Quite often,

203
00:16:07,016 --> 00:16:08,654
she keeps to herself.

204
00:16:09,830 --> 00:16:10,830
And...

205
00:16:11,398 --> 00:16:12,997
all she does is draw.

206
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:16,940
I'm not sure

207
00:16:17,064 --> 00:16:20,412
whether something at home is making her stressed

208
00:16:20,772 --> 00:16:22,359
or upsetting her.

209
00:16:24,885 --> 00:16:27,195
She's been through a lot.

210
00:16:32,772 --> 00:16:34,372
But I'll try to take better care of her.

211
00:16:35,762 --> 00:16:36,762
Well...

212
00:16:36,969 --> 00:16:38,329
please take good care of her, sir.

213
00:16:40,527 --> 00:16:41,527
I will.

214
00:16:53,424 --> 00:16:54,488
So, about that case...

215
00:16:58,984 --> 00:17:00,250
the court has dismissed it.

216
00:17:04,996 --> 00:17:06,062
(Socialite Pruekpana cleared of charges)

217
00:17:06,086 --> 00:17:07,366
But you're not the one at fault.

218
00:17:13,664 --> 00:17:14,800
Don't blame yourself.

219
00:17:18,318 --> 00:17:19,318
Just let it go.

220
00:17:20,583 --> 00:17:21,663
You did the best you could.

221
00:17:24,083 --> 00:17:25,083
Did I?

222
00:17:27,973 --> 00:17:29,573
What about the victims who were scammed?

223
00:17:32,852 --> 00:17:33,972
What do you expect me to do?

224
00:17:34,530 --> 00:17:35,930
That's just how this country works.

225
00:17:37,291 --> 00:17:38,611
If you've got money, you get off.

226
00:17:42,413 --> 00:17:43,817
Have you signed for me?

227
00:17:46,545 --> 00:17:50,233
Pruek said he only needs a little more money.

228
00:17:51,319 --> 00:17:53,277
You know I'm finally getting somewhere.

229
00:17:54,687 --> 00:17:56,130
And this business

230
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:57,697
could take us a long way.

231
00:18:02,348 --> 00:18:03,523
But this house...

232
00:18:03,862 --> 00:18:04,862
Honey.

233
00:18:06,604 --> 00:18:08,386
Do you trust me?

234
00:18:09,398 --> 00:18:10,918
I know it'll succeed

235
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:14,656
if we work together.

236
00:18:19,729 --> 00:18:20,916
Trust me.

237
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:26,687
All right.

238
00:18:27,691 --> 00:18:28,983
Yeah, thank you.

239
00:18:56,845 --> 00:18:58,731
That's an oddly designed stuffed animal.

240
00:18:59,266 --> 00:19:00,409
Oh, Cherd.

241
00:19:03,202 --> 00:19:05,046
(Manager Room)

242
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:10,890
Are you tired?

243
00:19:11,528 --> 00:19:12,528
Yeah.

244
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:13,840
Lately,

245
00:19:14,656 --> 00:19:16,516
we've been short on night-shift staff.

246
00:19:18,121 --> 00:19:20,242
New people join and leave soon after.

247
00:19:21,033 --> 00:19:22,217
It's hard to find replacements.

248
00:19:22,241 --> 00:19:23,429
No one's applying at all.

249
00:19:27,279 --> 00:19:28,447
But the pay is so good.

250
00:19:29,518 --> 00:19:31,038
It probably isn't hard to find people.

251
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:32,762
You still don't know

252
00:19:33,350 --> 00:19:34,805
that not everyone can see

253
00:19:35,181 --> 00:19:36,501
the job ad?

254
00:19:40,483 --> 00:19:42,043
Especially for our store's night shift.

255
00:19:45,208 --> 00:19:46,560
Not everyone can see it?

256
00:19:46,938 --> 00:19:47,454
Yeah.

257
00:19:47,852 --> 00:19:48,852
That's right.

258
00:19:53,581 --> 00:19:54,581
This store

259
00:19:55,709 --> 00:19:56,709
chooses the people.

260
00:19:57,641 --> 00:19:58,641
Chooses them?

261
00:19:59,886 --> 00:20:00,886
How?

262
00:20:02,295 --> 00:20:04,513
What do you think this store really is?

263
00:20:08,403 --> 00:20:09,403
It's...

264
00:20:10,368 --> 00:20:12,281
a place that connects the world of the living

265
00:20:13,162 --> 00:20:14,454
to the world of the dead?

266
00:20:16,214 --> 00:20:17,226
Well...

267
00:20:18,277 --> 00:20:19,608
You could look at it that way.

268
00:20:20,196 --> 00:20:22,474
But I see this store as

269
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:25,026
something like a convenience store

270
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:26,703
for people who have died.

271
00:20:27,749 --> 00:20:29,351
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

272
00:20:29,451 --> 00:20:30,529
Actually, I don't think

273
00:20:31,077 --> 00:20:33,157
the dead are all that different from people like us.

274
00:20:33,205 --> 00:20:35,274
They miss the food they used to eat,

275
00:20:35,810 --> 00:20:37,853
the things they used to use,

276
00:20:38,568 --> 00:20:39,728
and when they want something,

277
00:20:39,857 --> 00:20:41,306
they stop by this store to buy it.

278
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,343
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

279
00:20:43,486 --> 00:20:44,780
Or maybe

280
00:20:44,968 --> 00:20:46,228
they come back

281
00:20:47,525 --> 00:20:50,769
because there's something they can't let go of,

282
00:20:51,232 --> 00:20:52,498
something left unresolved.

283
00:20:55,817 --> 00:20:56,817
Something like that.

284
00:21:21,610 --> 00:21:22,708
Oh, Nava.

285
00:21:24,516 --> 00:21:26,703
I was only putting it away.

286
00:21:26,844 --> 00:21:28,244
I wasn't going to take it anywhere.

287
00:21:29,527 --> 00:21:30,871
He said he doesn't like it.

288
00:21:52,567 --> 00:21:53,567
That crazy kid

289
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:56,027
gets stranger and stranger every day.

290
00:23:05,526 --> 00:23:06,526
That little weirdo.

291
00:23:15,712 --> 00:23:17,723
Ouch.

292
00:23:17,890 --> 00:23:19,499
Ouch. It hurts.

293
00:23:19,798 --> 00:23:20,470
It's me.

294
00:23:20,703 --> 00:23:21,703
Hey.

295
00:23:23,015 --> 00:23:24,015
Come on.

296
00:23:24,379 --> 00:23:25,379
Sorry.

297
00:23:25,622 --> 00:23:26,622
Good.

298
00:23:27,073 --> 00:23:28,073
When did you get here?

299
00:23:28,219 --> 00:23:29,366
Come on, bro.

300
00:23:29,504 --> 00:23:30,672
I've been here a while.

301
00:23:31,471 --> 00:23:33,226
Didn't you hear my car?

302
00:23:34,954 --> 00:23:35,535
Sorry.

303
00:23:35,962 --> 00:23:37,071
I got carried away.

304
00:23:39,530 --> 00:23:40,530
Carried away?

305
00:23:42,367 --> 00:23:43,367
I used to be a cop.

306
00:23:44,117 --> 00:23:45,962
Whoa, that's so cool.

307
00:23:46,090 --> 00:23:47,090
It's not cool.

308
00:23:47,925 --> 00:23:49,685
I'm just trying to make it through each day.

309
00:23:52,404 --> 00:23:53,404
Working here,

310
00:23:53,905 --> 00:23:55,471
just surviving is good enough, bro.

311
00:23:59,170 --> 00:24:00,370
Don't do that again. It hurts.

312
00:24:00,884 --> 00:24:01,884
Sorry.

313
00:24:09,323 --> 00:24:10,643
I've finished checking the stock.

314
00:24:10,870 --> 00:24:11,870
Anything else to do?

315
00:24:12,011 --> 00:24:13,011
I don't think so.

316
00:24:14,395 --> 00:24:16,902
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

317
00:24:33,997 --> 00:24:34,997
Metha.

318
00:24:44,548 --> 00:24:45,598
Why are you here?

319
00:24:46,292 --> 00:24:47,292
And...

320
00:24:48,751 --> 00:24:50,116
how's Nava doing?

321
00:24:54,082 --> 00:24:56,679
I know I left you and Nava, but...

322
00:24:57,762 --> 00:24:58,946
I didn't mean to.

323
00:25:01,648 --> 00:25:02,085
I...

324
00:25:02,266 --> 00:25:03,648
I really wanted to come see you.

325
00:25:04,656 --> 00:25:06,282
I've always wanted to come see you.

326
00:25:07,157 --> 00:25:08,693
I really wanted to, but...

327
00:25:09,093 --> 00:25:10,133
I didn't have the courage.

328
00:25:10,924 --> 00:25:11,924
I'm sorry.

329
00:25:12,788 --> 00:25:13,788
It's okay, Nam.

330
00:25:14,143 --> 00:25:15,263
You don't have to apologize.

331
00:25:15,423 --> 00:25:16,618
I'm sorry, Metha.

332
00:25:22,391 --> 00:25:23,391
Metha.

333
00:25:25,729 --> 00:25:26,119
Yeah?

334
00:25:26,689 --> 00:25:27,689
Is something wrong?

335
00:25:29,324 --> 00:25:30,324
She's someone I know.

336
00:25:32,630 --> 00:25:34,310
Can I step away and talk to her privately?

337
00:25:38,587 --> 00:25:39,587
Someone you know?

338
00:25:41,330 --> 00:25:42,770
There's something we need to settle.

339
00:25:43,092 --> 00:25:44,852
I don't want to disturb the other customers.

340
00:25:47,486 --> 00:25:48,486
Okay.

341
00:25:56,965 --> 00:25:58,778
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

342
00:25:58,826 --> 00:25:59,826
Hey!

343
00:25:59,866 --> 00:26:00,866
You.

344
00:26:01,807 --> 00:26:03,287
Hurry up and put the money in my bag!

345
00:26:04,828 --> 00:26:05,828
Move it!

346
00:26:09,933 --> 00:26:10,933
Hey.

347
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,037
I said put the money in my bag!

348
00:26:14,733 --> 00:26:15,733
Hurry!

349
00:26:16,637 --> 00:26:17,213
Are you even human?

350
00:26:17,459 --> 00:26:19,760
Stop asking. Put the money in the bag now!

351
00:26:22,277 --> 00:26:23,277
I'll go get it.

352
00:26:23,717 --> 00:26:24,717
Hurry.

353
00:26:33,350 --> 00:26:34,350
You.

354
00:26:34,715 --> 00:26:35,835
What are you trying to pull?

355
00:26:41,068 --> 00:26:42,628
I told you to put the money in the bag!

356
00:26:42,705 --> 00:26:44,108
Or this woman dies!

357
00:26:44,796 --> 00:26:45,796
Now!

358
00:26:45,972 --> 00:26:46,972
Metha.

359
00:27:31,627 --> 00:27:34,032
I said put the money in the bag, or this woman dies!

360
00:27:34,323 --> 00:27:35,323
Hurry!

361
00:27:36,558 --> 00:27:36,958
Metha.

362
00:27:37,118 --> 00:27:37,571
Hurry up.

363
00:27:37,596 --> 00:27:37,947
Okay.

364
00:27:38,374 --> 00:27:38,672
Got it.

365
00:27:38,768 --> 00:27:39,768
Now!

366
00:27:39,862 --> 00:27:40,862
Dear, help me.

367
00:27:41,984 --> 00:27:42,984
Move it.

368
00:27:43,659 --> 00:27:44,921
Hurry up, man.

369
00:27:45,310 --> 00:27:46,310
I'll really shoot.

370
00:28:01,295 --> 00:28:02,345
What are you up to?

371
00:28:03,647 --> 00:28:04,671
Is this all you've got?

372
00:28:05,497 --> 00:28:06,497
You two,

373
00:28:06,567 --> 00:28:07,969
get away from the counter!

374
00:28:08,628 --> 00:28:09,628
I can't.

375
00:28:09,926 --> 00:28:11,006
What are you talking about?

376
00:28:14,742 --> 00:28:15,742
Store rules.

377
00:28:16,529 --> 00:28:17,345
The counter can't be left unattended

378
00:28:17,369 --> 00:28:18,489
for more than three minutes.

379
00:28:18,630 --> 00:28:20,305
I don't care about your stupid rules.

380
00:28:20,875 --> 00:28:21,905
I said back off!

381
00:28:23,622 --> 00:28:24,622
I'm counting to three.

382
00:28:26,756 --> 00:28:27,756
Alright.

383
00:28:28,260 --> 00:28:28,852
Move.

384
00:28:28,905 --> 00:28:29,905
Got it.

385
00:28:32,143 --> 00:28:32,721
Hurry up!

386
00:28:32,746 --> 00:28:33,746
I'm moving.

387
00:28:35,905 --> 00:28:37,142
Both of you, sit down.

388
00:28:38,113 --> 00:28:39,113
Now!

389
00:28:40,273 --> 00:28:41,745
Don't try anything funny.

390
00:28:42,102 --> 00:28:43,342
Come on. You're coming with me.

391
00:28:58,442 --> 00:29:00,308
What? That's all you've got?

392
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:04,958
Hey.

393
00:29:05,668 --> 00:29:07,038
Metha, time's almost up.

394
00:29:07,062 --> 00:29:08,062
What's with these lights?

395
00:29:10,505 --> 00:29:11,505
I'll go.

396
00:29:15,641 --> 00:29:16,641
Hey!

397
00:29:17,688 --> 00:29:18,755
I told you not to move.

398
00:29:29,167 --> 00:29:31,252
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

399
00:29:32,249 --> 00:29:33,249
Put the gun down

400
00:29:33,740 --> 00:29:34,972
and release the hostage.

401
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:37,655
You put your gun down.

402
00:29:38,567 --> 00:29:39,740
Or this woman dies!

403
00:29:40,199 --> 00:29:41,199
Hurry.

404
00:29:43,976 --> 00:29:45,139
Move it, old man.

405
00:29:46,296 --> 00:29:47,296
Put the gun down.

406
00:29:50,205 --> 00:29:51,205
Now!

407
00:30:03,814 --> 00:30:04,814
What's with these lights?

408
00:30:05,056 --> 00:30:06,056
Hey.

409
00:30:06,480 --> 00:30:07,480
What's going on?

410
00:30:17,376 --> 00:30:18,390
Hey, Captain.

411
00:30:19,190 --> 00:30:19,776
Oh, Sergeant.

412
00:30:20,041 --> 00:30:21,961
You're about to be promoted to inspector, right?

413
00:30:22,381 --> 00:30:23,381
Oh.

414
00:30:23,538 --> 00:30:24,698
I'm not quite there yet, sir.

415
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:26,872
If not you, Captain,

416
00:30:27,346 --> 00:30:28,346
then who?

417
00:30:29,320 --> 00:30:31,256
I trained you myself.

418
00:30:33,162 --> 00:30:34,162
But it's a good thing.

419
00:30:34,586 --> 00:30:36,080
We're all getting old.

420
00:30:37,477 --> 00:30:38,544
We'll be retiring soon.

421
00:30:40,305 --> 00:30:42,652
Then we can relax and look after our grandkids.

422
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:49,704
Here.

423
00:30:50,248 --> 00:30:51,248
My granddaughter.

424
00:30:52,152 --> 00:30:53,389
She was born just last week.

425
00:30:53,837 --> 00:30:54,837
Wow.

426
00:30:55,352 --> 00:30:56,352
She's cute, Sergeant.

427
00:30:57,240 --> 00:30:58,240
Congratulations.

428
00:30:58,841 --> 00:31:00,985
Prawet One, reporting incident 241.

429
00:31:01,353 --> 00:31:02,852
Location, Yaowarat Gold Shop.

430
00:31:03,049 --> 00:31:04,879
One armed suspect, unknown weapon.

431
00:31:04,932 --> 00:31:05,551
We've got a call.

432
00:31:05,631 --> 00:31:06,644
Units are on their way.

433
00:31:06,719 --> 00:31:07,719
Stop.

434
00:31:09,216 --> 00:31:10,696
Aren't your reports still unfinished?

435
00:31:12,298 --> 00:31:13,858
Let the experienced officers handle it.

436
00:31:14,331 --> 00:31:16,291
Save your energy for your promotion to inspector.

437
00:31:32,507 --> 00:31:32,864
Hey.

438
00:31:33,510 --> 00:31:34,672
Stop! Don't move!

439
00:31:35,659 --> 00:31:36,659
Drop your weapon!

440
00:31:37,222 --> 00:31:38,379
I said put the gun down.

441
00:31:38,704 --> 00:31:39,704
Or this woman dies!

442
00:31:39,973 --> 00:31:40,848
Release the hostage!

443
00:31:40,923 --> 00:31:41,712
Hurry up!

444
00:31:41,765 --> 00:31:42,683
You can't get away.

445
00:31:42,784 --> 00:31:43,784
Hurry!

446
00:31:43,867 --> 00:31:44,867
Put the gun down!

447
00:31:46,758 --> 00:31:47,758
Idiot.

448
00:32:02,296 --> 00:32:05,315
One officer has died at the scene.

449
00:32:05,678 --> 00:32:07,262
The suspect has now fled.

450
00:32:07,336 --> 00:32:09,351
Report any suspect immediately.

451
00:32:09,570 --> 00:32:10,719
The suspect is armed.

452
00:32:18,346 --> 00:32:19,346
Hey.

453
00:32:19,775 --> 00:32:20,775
What?

454
00:32:29,125 --> 00:32:30,125
Hey.

455
00:32:33,152 --> 00:32:34,309
Aren't you dead?

456
00:32:34,565 --> 00:32:36,421
You remember now?

457
00:32:37,329 --> 00:32:38,329
Go.

458
00:32:40,273 --> 00:32:41,273
Go.

459
00:32:41,798 --> 00:32:43,761
Using a hostage again, huh?

460
00:32:43,814 --> 00:32:44,814
Go.

461
00:32:44,913 --> 00:32:45,913
This time

462
00:32:46,830 --> 00:32:48,905
you're not getting away.

463
00:32:49,048 --> 00:32:50,048
Go!

464
00:32:57,733 --> 00:32:58,143
Hey.

465
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,842
Where did he go?

466
00:33:01,317 --> 00:33:02,317
Hey.

467
00:33:06,665 --> 00:33:07,665
Nam.

468
00:33:13,401 --> 00:33:14,401
Hey.

469
00:33:15,288 --> 00:33:16,750
You're under arrest!

470
00:33:16,878 --> 00:33:17,481
Don't.

471
00:33:17,808 --> 00:33:18,808
A ghost!

472
00:33:19,480 --> 00:33:20,640
I need to take the money too.

473
00:33:20,691 --> 00:33:22,424
Hey. Help.

474
00:33:22,646 --> 00:33:23,646
Hey. Open up.

475
00:33:23,851 --> 00:33:25,430
Who locked the door? Open it.

476
00:33:27,090 --> 00:33:27,666
Rule number eight.

477
00:33:27,691 --> 00:33:29,972
Store property must not be taken for personal use

478
00:33:29,997 --> 00:33:31,949
or embezzled under any circumstances.

479
00:33:53,303 --> 00:33:54,455
I'll call an ambulance.

480
00:33:55,735 --> 00:33:56,735
Don't, Dear.

481
00:33:57,027 --> 00:33:58,027
Why not?

482
00:33:58,750 --> 00:33:59,769
We can call one first.

483
00:33:59,950 --> 00:34:00,410
I think there's still time.

484
00:34:00,435 --> 00:34:01,435
Dear.

485
00:34:08,422 --> 00:34:09,422
Don't.

486
00:34:14,022 --> 00:34:15,379
Why didn't you save me?

487
00:34:18,489 --> 00:34:19,956
Why did you let me die?

488
00:34:27,369 --> 00:34:28,369
Hey.

489
00:34:29,033 --> 00:34:30,233
What are you sitting here for?

490
00:34:32,017 --> 00:34:33,879
I'm gathering evidence on that Pruek guy.

491
00:34:34,156 --> 00:34:35,156
I'll help you, Nam.

492
00:34:40,033 --> 00:34:41,033
Mom.

493
00:34:44,314 --> 00:34:46,159
Are you going to let Metha die?

494
00:34:46,282 --> 00:34:48,783
Business investments always carry risks, Officer.

495
00:34:49,110 --> 00:34:50,262
Metha.

496
00:34:50,324 --> 00:34:51,324
Don't answer her.
